===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|undon}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ondōn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*andadōnaz}}, past participle of {{m|gem-pro|*andadōną|t=to undo}}, equivalent to {{af|en|undo|-en|id2=past participle|pos2=past participle ending}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|ontdaan|t=stripped, undone, upset}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not [[fastened]].
#: {{ux|en|Your flies are '''undone'''.}}
# [[ruined|Ruined]]; [[bring to nought|brought to nought]].
#: {{ux|en|Woe is me, for I am utterly '''undone'''!}}
#* {{RQ:Roethke Collected|Feud|4|Your hopes are murdered and '''undone'''.}}

